    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0153" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1180</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spencer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-02T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1918,
                                8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Repeat to Tokyo your March 1, 1 p.m. Instruct Drysdale to proceed westward toward
                    Irkutsk if he considers it safe to do so and report facts as to situations
                    especially verifying or correcting <pb facs="0154" n="64" xml:id="pg64"/> rumors
                    of the arming of German prisoners. Repeat to Tokyo for information all future
                    important telegrams relating to situation in Siberia and inform Department when
                    done.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
